  "nl_text": "The database schema named \"schemabench_0125\" consists of 16 tables. The primary function of this schema is to manage and store information related to a movie rental store.\n###Instruction:Thedatabasenameandwhatitisusedfor.\nThe database is named \"schemabench_0125\" and its primary function is to manage and store information related to a movie rental store. It includes details about actors, addresses, categories, cities, countries, customers, films, film actors, film categories, film text, inventory, languages, payments, rentals, staff, and stores. Each table represents a specific entity in the movie rental store, such as actors, addresses, categories, etc. The information in each table is used to provide a comprehensive overview of the store's operations, including inventory, customer information, rental history, staff details, and more.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThis project involves the Sakila test database, a fictional and simplified database designed to manage a video rental store. It contains data structures relevant to tracking movies, customers, rentals, and payments in a video rental business context.\n\nObjectives\n\nThe objective is to create a database system that efficiently manages various aspects of a video rental business, including movie information, inventory management, customer records, rental transactions, and related payments.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Store Managers: Oversee store operations and manage inventory.\n- Staff: Handle customer interactions, process rentals, and manage transactions.\n- Customers: Rent movies and interact with store services.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Movie Management:\n   - Store and manage details about films, including titles, descriptions, release years, languages, ratings, and special features.\n   - Categorize films into different genres using a category system.\n\n2. Inventory Management:\n   - Track inventory of films across different stores.\n\n3. Customer Management:\n   - Maintain records of customer details including addresses, contact information, and rental history.\n   - Manage active status of customers.\n\n4. Rental Processing:\n   - Record rental transactions including rental dates and return dates.\n   - Associate each rental with a customer and store staff member.\n\n5. Payment Processing:\n   - Process payments linked to rental transactions.\n   - Store details of payment amounts and dates.\n\n6. Staff Management:\n   - Manage staff details for operational purposes.\n   - Assign staff members to stores.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Database Integrity: Ensure referential integrity through the use of foreign keys.\n- User Access Control: Allow different levels of access for managers, staff, and customers.\n- Scalability: Support potential increase in data and user interactions.\n- Data Consistency: Maintain data accuracy with constraints and default values.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_deepseek/0125.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0125\nCREATE TABLE `actor` (\n  `actor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `first_name` varchar(45) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(45) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`actor_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `address` (\n  `address_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `address2` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `district` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `city_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `postal_code` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`address_id`),\n  FOREIGN KEY (`city_id`) REFERENCES `city` (`city_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `category` (\n  `category_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(25) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`category_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `city` (\n  `city_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `country_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`city_id`),\n  FOREIGN KEY (`country_id`) REFERENCES `country` (`country_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `country` (\n  `country_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`country_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `store_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `first_name` varchar(45) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(45) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `active` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`),\n  FOREIGN KEY (`store_id`) REFERENCES `store` (`store_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  FOREIGN KEY (`address_id`) REFERENCES `address` (`address_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `film` (\n  `film_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `release_year` year(4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `language_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `original_language_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `rental_duration` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '3',\n  `rental_rate` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL DEFAULT '4.99',\n  `length` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `replacement_cost` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL DEFAULT '19.99',\n  `rating` enum('G','PG','PG-13','R','NC-17') DEFAULT NULL,\n  `special_features` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`film_id`),\n  FOREIGN KEY (`language_id`) REFERENCES `language` (`language_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  FOREIGN KEY (`original_language_id`) REFERENCES `language` (`language_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `film_actor` (\n  `film_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `actor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`film_id`, `actor_id`),\n  FOREIGN KEY (`film_id`) REFERENCES `film` (`film_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  FOREIGN KEY (`actor_id`) REFERENCES `actor` (`actor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `film_category` (\n  `film_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `category_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`film_id`, `category_id`),\n  FOREIGN KEY (`film_id`) REFERENCES `film` (`film_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  FOREIGN KEY (`category_id`) REFERENCES `category` (`category_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `film_text` (\n  `film_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `text` mediumtext DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`film_id`),\n  FOREIGN KEY (`film_id`) REFERENCES `film` (`film_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `inventory` (\n  `inventory_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `film_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `store_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `last_update` timestamp NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`inventory_id`),\n  FOREIGN KEY (`film_id`) REFERENCES `film` (`film_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  FOREIGN KEY (`store_id`) REFERENCES `store` (`store_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `language` (\n  `language_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`language_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `payment` (\n  `payment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rental_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  `payment_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`payment_id`),\n  FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  FOREIGN KEY (`staff_id`) REFERENCES `staff` (`staff_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  FOREIGN KEY (`rental_id`) REFERENCES `rental` (`rental_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `rental` (\n  `rental_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rental_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `inventory_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `return_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`rental_id`),\n  FOREIGN KEY (`inventory_id`) REFERENCES `inventory` (`inventory_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  FOREIGN KEY (`staff_id`) REFERENCES `staff` (`staff_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `staff` (\n  `staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `first_name` varchar(45) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(45) NOT NULL,\n  `address_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `store_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `active` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`staff_id`),\n  FOREIGN KEY (`address_id`) REFERENCES `address` (`address_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  FOREIGN KEY (`store_id`) REFERENCES `store` (`store_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `store` (\n  `store_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `manager_staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `address_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`store_id`),\n  FOREIGN KEY (`manager_staff_id`) REFERENCES `staff` (`staff_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  FOREIGN KEY (`address_id`) REFERENCES `address` (`address_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
